WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.200
We look at just two simple sets in this video.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.920
Set 'P' which has one, two and three as its elements,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.220
and set 'Q' which has one, two,

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.680
three, four, and five as its elements.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.020
Understand the elements well.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.920
This has one, two and three

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.540
and this one has one, two, three, four and five.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.840
This is a part of this.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.820
And that’s why we say set 'P' is a part of set 'Q'.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.100
And we learned in the previous video,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.940
that 'part of' also means subsets.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.520
So we can say that set 'P' is a subset of set 'Q'.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.740
Do we have a symbol to represent this?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.400
Yes, it's written like this.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.580
'P' is a subset of 'Q'.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.900
The letter 'U' is sleeping on this line.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.500
So when is 'P' a subset of a 'Q'?

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.240
Set 'P' is a subset of set 'Q'

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.880
when every element in 'P' is also present in 'Q'.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.520
Look at the elements.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.740
Every element in 'P' is also present in 'Q'.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.520
But this statement raises a new query.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.040
Look at sets 'C' and 'D'.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.560
Set 'C' has four, five and six, as its elements.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.960
And set 'D' has four, six and five as its elements.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.880
Both the sets have the same elements which makes them equal.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.620
But every element in set 'C' is also present in set 'D'.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.740
Based on the definition we can say that set 'C' is a subset of set 'D'.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.740
This also tells us something more!

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.680
It tells us that every set is a subset of itself.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.780
'P' is a subset of 'P'.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.740
'Q' is a subset of 'Q'. And so on...

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.260
For some reason, this does not seem entirely correct

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.160
and that give rise to a new concept of proper subset.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.580
Look at sets 'P' and 'Q'.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.200
Set 'P' is a part of set 'Q'

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.320
but there is at least one element in set 'Q' which is not present

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.920
and in set 'P'.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.240
We say that set 'P' is a proper subset of set 'Q'.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.440
This sign indicates proper subset.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.320
And this tells us that all elements of 'P' are present in set 'Q',

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.620
but there is at least one element in 'Q'

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.980
Which is not present in 'P'.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.640
We can see that 4 and 5 are not present in 'P'.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.780
So that's the concept of a proper subset.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.340
Sometimes it is also referred to as the strict subset.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.140
Can we say 'C' is a proper subset of 'D'?

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:58.480
Think about it,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.280
that would be incorrect since there is no element in 'D',

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.480
which is not a part of 'C'.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.500
There has to be at least one such element.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.340
That's the only difference between a subset,

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.440
and a proper subset.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.560
Just one last thing we need to understand.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.080
Just as we say 'P' is a proper subset of 'Q'.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:25.200
We can also say that set 'Q' is a super set of set 'P'.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.640
This symbol is used to represent super set.

